# vacti arsenal - WEB-LEAN (baked default, ENGINE_CAPABILITIES=web,infra)
#
# Derived from the engine's packaging/bootstrap-apt.sh APT_PACKAGES, minus the
# per-vertical gated sets (source/mobile/ios/re) which the runtime self-heal
# fetches post-boot only when a wider capability is advertised. One package per
# line; blank lines and # comments are ignored by gen-live-build-list.sh and by
# golden-image/build-golden.sh.
#
# The ~6 tools NOT in Debian main (nuclei httpx-toolkit naabu feroxbuster
# seclists commix) resolve from the pinned Kali apt source (Option A) or the
# engine's go/git/release fallbacks (Option B, VACTI_NO_KALI_REPO=1).

# --- Scanners / recon CORE ---
nmap
nuclei
httpx-toolkit
naabu
subfinder
ffuf
gobuster
dirsearch
sqlmap
weevely
whatweb
commix
dnsx
katana
trufflehog
feroxbuster

# --- Content-discovery wordlists (seclists is load-bearing; dirb is fallback) ---
seclists
dirb

# --- Base / runtime ---
default-mysql-client
nftables
jq
curl
wget
git
build-essential
ca-certificates
xvfb
fonts-noto
fonts-noto-cjk
fonts-noto-color-emoji
pipx
golang-go
ripgrep
fd-find
openssh-server
adb
xz-utils
socat
netcat-openbsd
default-jre-headless
unzip
binutils
python3-venv
python3-full

# --- TLS / network inspection (small, broadly used by tls-review & probers) ---
sslscan
testssl.sh

# --- Anti-OOM backstops (see distro/golden-image/oom/) ---
# zram compressed RAM swap (primary cushion) + earlyoom userspace OOM killer
# backstop. Their config is shipped as copy-in drop-ins by build-golden.sh.
systemd-zram-generator
earlyoom

# --- Client-VPN clients (an engagement runs behind the client's VPN) ---
openconnect
openfortivpn
openvpn
wireguard-tools
strongswan
strongswan-swanctl

# --- Evidence / screenshot pipeline ---
imagemagick
xdotool
x11-xserver-utils
qterminal
sshpass
tmux

# --- Chromium ---
# vacti-engine-chromium removed: the engine .deb bundles Chromium via
# playwright-core's pinned build 1228; no separate apt package exists.
#
# The bundled Chromium still needs its shared-library deps present on the rootfs
# to launch headless. Debian 13 genericcloud is very thin, so make them EXPLICIT
# instead of relying on them arriving as recommends (a missing libnss3/libgbm1
# is the classic headless-launch failure). Debian 13 (trixie) completed the
# 64-bit time_t transition, so several of these ship under t64 names
# (libasound2t64, libatk1.0-0t64, libatk-bridge2.0-0t64, libcups2t64); the
# per-package best-effort install in provision.sh tolerates a name that is not
# present on a given point release.
libnss3
libgbm1
libasound2t64
libatk1.0-0t64
libatk-bridge2.0-0t64
libcups2t64
libdrm2
libxkbcommon0
libxcomposite1
libxdamage1
libxrandr2
libxfixes3
libpango-1.0-0
libcairo2
